:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625994} {:answer/id #uuid "67ca1858-e093-5357-813b-633caca5e7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{43}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625996} {:answer/id #uuid "b2295432-a61a-5f8a-be1d-cfbe48b8e009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{41}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626009}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625982} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad1d8acd-2cf7-5069-acc5-2df62df87316" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6e8e137a-50f5-5e48-bb22-9bc5d8049e9e" :question/problem "The vector $c$ has magnitude $25$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$." :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $c$, we divide $c$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|}=\\frac{1}{25}c\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42d1cc97-2d5d-50d2-8baa-cbe11bda866c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\overrightarrow{CD}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625987} {:answer/id #uuid "660f4a55-420c-521c-9d02-470aa46174a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{21}\\overrightarrow{CD}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625995} {:answer/id #uuid "6f881937-5d95-587a-b2e0-9c45df79aa5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\overrightarrow{CD}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626000} {:answer/id #uuid "9a4fbb86-65cd-597c-af4a-05939da2cbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}\\overrightarrow{CD}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626005} {:answer/id #uuid "bd1a3461-9401-5758-b01e-1d4479dabd9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}\\overrightarrow{CD}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626011}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625995} :answer-field/id #uuid "477bab34-43c3-510f-9a8f-91541d80a375" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "825c2c4f-7d04-54ce-8658-f593b3c101ed" :question/problem "The vector $\\overrightarrow{CD}$ has magnitude $21$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overrightarrow{CD}$?" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\overrightarrow{CD}$, we divide $\\overrightarrow{CD}$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overrightarrow{CD}}{|\\,\\overrightarrow{CD}\\,|}=\\frac{1}{21}\\overrightarrow{CD}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5671e285-4ee2-5784-b83f-90f458ff0ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\overrightarrow{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625993} {:answer/id #uuid "6d695420-ae9e-5217-84d0-3af3355edf4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}\\overrightarrow{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625998} {:answer/id #uuid "75d9df89-f5d0-5229-8041-eabed02fa2f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}\\overrightarrow{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626001} {:answer/id #uuid "8adf885c-4b72-56b1-9c79-a514e76dcdf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}\\overrightarrow{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626003} {:answer/id #uuid "9fe703de-7c7f-59d3-8725-d19d9a399f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}\\overrightarrow{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626007}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626007} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3341bd-2a35-595f-acf3-3fe25448238a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cc948c95-5fd0-5a6d-9382-f5e704c3f5a9" :question/problem "The vector $\\overrightarrow{ST}$ has magnitude $15$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overrightarrow{ST}$?" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\overrightarrow{ST}$, we divide $\\overrightarrow{ST}$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overrightarrow{ST}}{|\\,\\overrightarrow{ST}\\,|}=\\frac{1}{15}\\overrightarrow{ST}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b8c7c5-f3a5-5874-9b3a-31f0a8efec1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625980} {:answer/id #uuid "0c9df639-b7a5-5bee-84bb-7261af1ba8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625981} {:answer/id #uuid "4d158cad-da79-5443-9647-d81369c64678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625991} {:answer/id #uuid "b8624a42-dcc9-5ec6-8ae9-ad639000313f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626010} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b93d02-8a93-5757-a0b1-5588720131da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626010} :answer-field/id #uuid "46644b4d-5f91-5b29-9966-ff50c1dcacac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d378a603-345c-51cb-9571-ef055772f412" :question/problem "The vector $a$ has magnitude $9$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$." :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $a$, we divide $a$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a}{|\\,a\\,|}=\\frac{1}{9}a\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef06d92-01a8-547d-b825-ee32e9d59c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626959}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626959} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcad0e2-4981-5e4c-961e-4423955b75f1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626966}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1626871e-9f91-5ee8-abbe-a161bda4b920" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the left and has magnitude $\\sqrt{3}$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $\\sqrt{6}.$ Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to $a+b$ and has the same direction as $a+b.$\n\nType $a$ and $b$ to represent the vectors $a$ and $b,$ respectively.\n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$\n\n![](images/97/97b9233250b17231f8a032f1c4a15c6ff91b861a503c7a1eb50f54aa4dba9af3.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nThe given directions are perpendicular, so we obtain a right triangle. We can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=(\\sqrt{3})^2+(\\sqrt{6})^2\\\\\n&=3+6\\\\\n&=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{9}=3\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{3}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "395529ae-78bf-5ebc-a4d0-8973180776f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{55}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626950}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626950} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f864af4-49b9-582f-8113-1b6f259c7527" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a4e66893-29d1-52d5-a6ef-253fa068876f" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the left and has magnitude $3 \\sqrt{3}$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $2 \\sqrt{7}.$ Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to $a+b$ and has the same direction as $a+b.$\n\nType $a$ and $b$ to represent the vectors $a$ and $b,$ respectively.\n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$\n\n![](images/ae/ae50887736a1299ced9ed6dfa13c31b4494eb24a68fffc482eca525ea71bc162.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nThe given directions are perpendicular, so we obtain a right triangle. We can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=(3 \\sqrt{3})^2+(2 \\sqrt{7})^2\\\\\n&=27+28\\\\\n&=55\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{55}=\\sqrt{55}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{55}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f32ba1-4503-5eff-a636-2d97a6d1a536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{673}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626944} {:answer/id #uuid "308f5adf-f413-5e24-a48c-5637ff4a19af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{881}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626948} {:answer/id #uuid "364a2f0a-7bad-5950-9342-2922b0308dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{194}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626949} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3f3035-a840-5612-8889-7af1d37cf076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{328}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626952} {:answer/id #uuid "8058d22d-9032-5797-b14a-e8c6029f753b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{202}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626956}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626952} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a76d5b-cfa5-5166-aa4b-85c7587b64b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d530488d-eb9b-5b16-bff0-3d454ba24a72" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $18$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $2.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$\n\n![](images/a3/a3f2345bc172424550ae61158e8ae1e8a9d8872b0a1e877c6eae66fa6f6a4b60.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nThe given directions are perpendicular, so we obtain a right triangle. We can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=(18)^2+(2)^2\\\\\n&=324+4\\\\\n&=328\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{328}=2 \\sqrt{82}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{82}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2599a685-f05e-56a1-82ec-19761ef7cc32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{23}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626947}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626947} :answer-field/id #uuid "e360bb08-089f-5626-a275-f023e8ec3587" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d86ab3de-fe8f-5090-9017-d119317031c7" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the left and has magnitude $\\sqrt{17}$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $\\sqrt{6}.$ Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to $a+b$ and has the same direction as $a+b.$\n\nType $a$ and $b$ to represent the vectors $a$ and $b,$ respectively.\n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$\n\n![](images/de/def8d44d6e773c9385c62559fccd83ea638924222fcce09b05806bf99beb71ac.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nThe given directions are perpendicular, so we obtain a right triangle. We can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=(\\sqrt{17})^2+(\\sqrt{6})^2\\\\\n&=17+6\\\\\n&=23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{23}=\\sqrt{23}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{23}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64cca3f0-adb3-5fbb-ae61-a7e975d82ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{1466}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626953} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6c1e39-e004-5138-ad95-47ecb7474c20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{1170}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626954} {:answer/id #uuid "7138ea1b-fa49-5c43-aada-163ea7c42993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{117}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626955} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1e60a7-84fe-5435-b74c-92a5f181797b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{1010}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626957} {:answer/id #uuid "bc44e53b-c184-567a-8a5e-f475783131b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{1258}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626960}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626957} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0b1bae-7085-5ace-9295-d5031f0b289f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f1f0527e-eca5-5ae8-9f80-c6c66a72be78" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $13$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $29.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$\n\n![](images/98/98b4899d5f2729612b63f6e37d24510a07ff7fe899f4b437f60278d7805c1029.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nThe given directions are perpendicular, so we obtain a right triangle. We can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=(13)^2+(29)^2\\\\\n&=169+841\\\\\n&=1010\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{1010}=\\sqrt{1010}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1010}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186630234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6517970f-34a1-5af8-bce8-e3f17e565294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629769} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7a5947-04d6-5f13-97e0-d8ab5101a94d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629945} {:answer/id #uuid "de3b5f17-97f3-566e-aa1a-0cc610f6dc83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629996} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a32ffd-1c65-5963-b0ed-f305e79bd216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630013} {:answer/id #uuid "fceceea3-a695-55cd-bb1f-833e66c4bee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630053}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629945} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e80db56-d1b9-5c83-bfa9-a4429b611c1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186630066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a4d452bd-a709-5b30-85de-4e9793ebbeb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-71104" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,DFG$, if $D(1,0,0)$, $F(1,2,1)$, $G(1,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DG}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =(i+2j+k)-i \\\\  & =2j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DG} & =g-d \\\\  & =(i+3j+k)-i \\\\  & =3j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,3,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DG} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1)i-(0\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1)j+(0\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-i \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DG}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DG}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,DFG$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186633605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9893ffbd-33dd-5839-8a04-575c481ecf30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633196}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186633196} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec524b6e-9afd-5b5e-bdb9-f2aa8533ecd4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186633491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f98382c9-0130-5b4a-bffb-6342109486f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-275260" :question/problem "Let $g=\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ t \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $h=\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ If $g⊥h,$ then $t=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =t\\cdot t+t\\cdot (-4)+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-4t+4 \\\\  & =(t-2)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ (t-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ t-2 & =0 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
